  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Ongoing central chest discomfort described as pressure/\"someone sitting on my chest\", started while gardening a couple of hours ago.\n- Symptoms: Chest pressure (mid-sternal, diffuse), onset a few hours ago while kneeling/gardening; still present at time of call. Radiation to left arm and shoulder. Associated nausea (no vomiting), diaphoresis, shortness of breath, sensation of palpitations (says heart is beating a bit faster). Severity: enough concern to call ambulance; patient and clinician worry about heart attack. Aggravating/alleviating factors: started with mild physical activity (gardening) but not strenuous; no clear alleviating factors reported.\n- Past medical history: Hypertension (patient reports \"high blood\"), no diabetes. No prior similar episodes (first time experiencing this).\n- Medications / Allergies: Medications not listed. Allergy: aspirin (mild allergic reaction with swelling; not life-threatening but should be communicated to hospital).\n- Family / Social history: Father died of a heart attack around age ~60; mother had \"some heart problems.\" Smokes ~10 cigarettes/day for 15 years. Drinks ~7–8 pints/week. Overweight. Lives alone. Works as a restaurant/sushi shop owner.\n- Vital signs / exam findings: None recorded in transcript (no pulse, BP, respiratory rate, oxygen saturation, or exam documented). Patient appears sweaty and short of breath per history.\n- Labs / imaging: None available in transcript. Clinician plans ECG and ambulance transport.\n",
